-- the measured shifts of leucine's protons, in hundredths of a ppm, from the standard random-coil table
-- (Wuthrich 1986, GGXA peptides at pH 7.0 and 35 C): the amide protons at 8.42, the alpha proton at
-- 4.38, the beta methylene reported as one value at 1.65, the gamma proton at 1.64, and the two delta
-- methyls at 0.94 and 0.90. The hydroxyl proton exchanges and is given its own value. The carbons,
-- nitrogen and oxygens are not protons and take 0; only the hydrogens are counted.
lu-shift : Leu → Nat
lu-shift x = case x of
  lu-c1 → 0
  lu-o1 → 0
  lu-o2 → 0
  lu-ho → 500
  lu-ca → 0
  lu-ha → 438
  lu-n → 0
  lu-hn1 → 842
  lu-hn2 → 842
  lu-cb → 0
  lu-hb1 → 165
  lu-hb2 → 165
  lu-cg → 0
  lu-hg → 164
  lu-cd1 → 0
  lu-d11 → 94
  lu-d12 → 94
  lu-d13 → 94
  lu-cd2 → 0
  lu-d21 → 90
  lu-d22 → 90
  lu-d23 → 90
